<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong Motor workers down tools.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong Motor workers down tools.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union workers at South Korea's Ssangyong Motor began an indefinite strike on Thursday in protest against passage of a new labour law, a senior union official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We stopped our production lines at 8.30 this morning (2330 GMT) right after the new labour law passed,&quot; union secretary Lee Jun-hee said by telephone.</p>
<p>Unions members were now holding a mass meeting, he said.</p>
